            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Dickinson's Later Years</strong><br>\nIn her later years, Dickinson's health deteriorated, which furthered her reclusive lifestyle. She continued to write poetry, but became increasingly withdrawn and introspective.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nAfter Dickinson's death on May 15, 1886, her family discovered her poems, which were published posthumously. They received widespread acclaim and made her one of America's most esteemed poets.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nToday, Dickinson is considered a pioneer of modern poetry due to her resistance to traditional poetic form and her exploration of complex themes within simple compositions.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
